 operations\n- **BiometricCredentials**: Data model for stored credentials (username, encrypted password, IV)\n- **BiometricAuthResult**: Sealed interface for authentication results\n\n### UI Layer\n- **BiometricSetupScreen**: Prompts user to enable biometric auth on first login\n- **LoginScreen**: Updated with biometric login button (fingerprint icon)\n- **LoginViewModel**: Extended to handle both standard and biometric login\n\n## User Flow\n\n1. **First Login**:\n - User enters username and password\n - After successful authentication, user is redirected to BiometricSetupScreen\n - User can enable biometric auth or skip\n - If enabled, biometric prompt appears to encrypt and store password\n - User is then redirected to Home\n\n2. **Subsequent Logins**:\n - Login screen shows fingerprint icon if biometric is enabled\n - User taps fingerprint icon\n - Biometric prompt appears\n - On successful authentication, password is decrypted and automatic login occurs\n - User can still use manual username/password login\n\n3. **Logout**:\n - Biometric credentials are cleared\n - Next login will prompt for biometric setup again\n\n## Security Features\n\n- **Android Keystore**: All encryption keys are stored in hardware-backed keystore\n- **AES-GCM Encryption**: Password is encrypted using AES with Galois/Counter Mode\n- **Biometric Required**: Key usage requires biometric authentication each time\n- **No Plain Text Storage**: Password is never stored in plain text\n- **Auto-cleanup**: Credentials are cleared on logout\n\n## Key Components\n\n### CryptoManager\n```kotlin\n// Generates or retrieves AES key from Android Keystore\nfun getOrCreateKey(): SecretKey\n\n// Returns cipher configured for encryption\nfun getEncryptCipher(): Cipher\n\n// Returns cipher configured for decryption with IV\nfun getDecryptCipher(iv: ByteArray): Cipher\n\n// Encrypts data and returns (encrypted, IV) pair\nfun encryptData(plaintext: String, cipher: Cipher): Pair<String, String>\n\n// Decrypts data using encrypted string and IV\nfun decryptData(encryptedData: String, iv: String): String\n```\n\n### BiometricAuthManager\n```kotlin\n// Checks if biometric hardware is available\nfun isBiometricAvailable(): Boolean\n\n// Checks if user has enrolled biometric credentials\nfun isBiometricEnrolled(): Boolean\n\n// Shows biometric prompt for encryption (setup flow)\nsuspend fun authenticateForEncryption(activity: FragmentActivity, password: String): BiometricAuthResult\n\n// Shows biometric prompt for decryption (login flow)\nsuspend fun authenticateForDecryption(activity: FragmentActivity, encryptedPassword: String, iv: String): BiometricAuthResult\n```\n\n## Dependencies Added\n\n```kotlin\n// gradle/libs.versions.toml\nbiometric = \"1.1.0\"\nandroidx-biometric = { group = \"androidx.biometric\", name = \"biometric\", version.ref = \"biometric\" }\n\n// app/build.gradle.kts\nimplementation(libs.androidx.biometric)\n```\n\n## Permissions\n\n```xml\n<!-- AndroidManifest.xml -->\n<uses-permission android:name=\"android.permission.USE_BIOMETRIC\" />\n```\n\n## Testing Notes\n\n- Minimum SDK: API 24 (Android 7.0)\n- Biometric Strong authentication required\n- Test on device with enrolled fingerprint/face\n- Use Android Emulator's virtual fingerprint sensor for testing\n\n## Error Handling\n\n- **NotAvailable**: Device doesn't support biometric authentication\n- **NotEnrolled**: User hasn't enrolled any biometric credentials\n- **Failure**: Authentication failed (incorrect biometric)\n- **Cancelled**: User cancelled the authentication\n- **Success**: Authentication succeeded, includes decrypted password\n\n## Future Enhancements\n\n- Allow user to disable biometric from settings\n- Support for biometric re-enrollment when device credentials change\n- Option to use device credentials (PIN/Pattern) as fallback\n- Biometric prompt customization per user preference\n"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","name":"write","tool_call_id":"toolu_01GUrAHmoABnZvZrFAAgHBPe","content":"Wrote con