## The Problem

The `BiometricAuthResult` sealed class appears to have multiple result types that are relevant at different layers:

1. **`EncryptionSuccess`** - This seems to be a low-level data layer result indicating "encryption completed successfully"
2. **`Success`** - This is what the ViewModel actually cares about - "the entire biometric setup operation succeeded"

The ViewModel is being forced to handle implementation details (`EncryptionSuccess`) that should have been abstracted away by the use case or repository layer.

## Proposed Solutions

### Option 1: Filter at the Use Case Layer (Recommended)
The **`SaveBiometricCredentialsUseCase`** should map `EncryptionSuccess` to `Success` before returning to the ViewModel. The use case would handle this transformation:

```kotlin
override suspend fun invoke(params: Params): Result<BiometricAuthResult, FeatureError> {
 val result = biometricGateway.saveBiometricCredentials(...)

 // Map low-level results to domain-appropriate results
 val domainResult = when (result) {
 is BiometricAuthResult.EncryptionSuccess -> BiometricAuthResult.Success(Unit)
 else -> result
 }

 return Result.Success(domainResult)
}
```

### Option 2: Use Case Returns Its Own Result Type
Create a domain-specific result type that only includes outcomes relevant to the business logic:

```kotlin
sealed interface BiometricSetupResult {
 data object Success
 data object NotAvailable
 data object NotEnrolled
 data object Cancelled
 data class Failure(val errorCode: Int?)
}
```

The use case would map from `BiometricAuthResult` (data layer) to `BiometricSetupResult` (domain layer).

### Option 3: Split the BiometricAuthResult
Have separate result types:
- `BiometricEncryptionResult` (used by data layer internally)
- `BiometricAuthResult` (used by domain/presentation layers)

## My Recommendation

**Option 1** is the cleanest with minimal changes. The use case is the perfect place to handle this transformation because:
- ✅ It keeps the ViewModel clean and focused on business logic
- ✅ It maintains proper layering - ViewModels don't know about encryption details
- ✅ The use case already wraps everything in `Result<BiometricAuthResult, FeatureError>`
- ✅ Minimal breaking changes

The same issue likely exists in **`LoginViewModel`** where it handles `EncryptionSuccess` as well (line 150-154), so we'd fix both.

What do you think? Should I proceed with **Option 1**?"}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"ok go with option 1"}],"context":[{"file_path":"app/src/main/java/com/afaneca/myfin/ui/login/biometric/BiometricSetupViewModel.kt","code_text":"package com.afaneca.myfin.ui.login.biometric

