Here's what's happening:
```kotlin
"" to statusResult.data.biometricStatus.canUseBiometric to statusResult.data.biometricStatus.isEnabled
// This is parsed as:
Pair(Pair("", canUseBiometric), isEnabled)
```

You have a few options to fix this:

**Option 1: Use Triple explicitly**
```kotlin
val statusResult = checkLoginStatusUseCase(Unit)
val (savedUsername, isBiometricAvailable, isBiometricEnabled) = when (statusResult) {
 is Result.Success -> {
 Triple("", statusResult.data.biometricStatus.canUseBiometric, statusResult.data.biometricStatus.isEnabled)
 }
 is Result.Error -> Triple("", false, false)
}
```

**Option 2: Destructure in two steps**
```kotlin
val statusResult = checkLoginStatusUseCase(Unit)
val (isBiometricAvailable, isBiometricEnabled) = when (statusResult) {
 is Result.Success -> {
 statusResult.data.biometricStatus.canUseBiometric to statusResult.data.biometricStatus.isEnabled
 }
 is Result.Error -> false to false
}
val savedUsername = ""
```

**Option 3: Use separate assignments (clearest)**
```kotlin
val statusResult = checkLoginStatusUseCase(Unit)
val savedUsername = ""
val isBiometricAvailable = when (statusResult) {
 is Result.Success -> statusResult.data.biometricStatus.canUseBiometric
 is Result.Error -> false
}
val isBiometricEnabled = when (statusResult) {
 is Result.Success -> statusResult.data.biometricStatus.isEnabled
 is Result.Error -> false
}
```

Which approach would you prefer? I'd recommend **Option 1** (Triple) if you want to keep the destructuring, or **Option 3** if you want maximum clarity."}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"option 1"}],"context":[{"file_path":"app/src/main/java/com/afaneca/myfin/ui/login/LoginViewModel.kt","code_text":"package com.afaneca.myfin.ui.login

