You update the state to `isBiometricEnabled = false` when the username changes (line 63), but then in `attemptLogin()` you're calling `checkLoginStatusUseCase` which checks the **actual stored credentials**, not what the state says.

So:
1. User changes username from "user1" to "user2"
2. State updates: `isBiometricEnabled = false` ✓ (fingerprint button hides)
3. User2 logs in successfully
4. `checkLoginStatusUseCase()` returns `isEnabled = true` ❌ (still sees user1's saved credentials!)
5. Code thinks user2 already has biometric enabled, skips setup

## The Fix

You should **trust the state** instead of re-checking. The state already knows whether the current user has biometric enabled:"}],"tool_calls":[{"id":"toolu_01237qaCBUhibw7dmUTrCCUp","type":"function","function":{"name":"read_file","arguments":"{"target_file": "app/src/main/java/com/afaneca/myfin/ui/login/LoginViewModel.kt", "offset": 108, "limit": 25}"}},{"id":"toolu_01VwRGmDZEc9nENgiubZSxtD","type":"function","function":{"name":"edit","arguments":"{"file_path": "C:/Users/afane/StudioProjects/myfin-android/android/app/src/main/java/com/afaneca/myfin/ui/login/LoginViewModel.kt", "old_string": " when (result) {\n is Result.Error -> handleLoginError(error = result.error)\n is Result.Success -> {\n // Check if this is first login (biometric not enabled yet)\n val statusResult = checkLoginStatusUseCase(Unit)\n val isBiometricEnabled = when (statusResult) {\n is Result.Success -> statusResult.data.biometricStatus.isEnabled\n is Result.Error -> false\n }\n\n if (!isBiometricEnabled && canUseBiometric) {\n // First login - redirect to biometric setup\n _mainState.update { it.copy(isFirstLogin = true) }\n _effect.tryEmit(LoginContract.Effect.GoToBiometricSetup(username, password))\n } else {\n // Not first login or biometric not available - go directly to home\n _effect.tryEmit(LoginContract.Effect.GoToHome)\n }\n }\n }", "new_string": " when (result) {\n is Result.Error -> handleLoginError(error = result.error)\n is Result.Success -> {\n // Check if this is first login (biometric not enabled yet)\n // Use state value which reflects whether current username has biometric enabled\n val isBiometricEnabled = mainState.value.isBiometricEnabled\n\n if (!isBiometricEnabled && canUseBiometric) {\n // First login - redirect to biometric setup\n _mainState.update { it.copy(isFirstLogin = true) }\n _effect.tryEmit(LoginContract.Effect.GoToBiometricSetup(username, password))\n } else {\n // Not first login or biometric not available - go directly to home\n _effect.tryEmit(LoginContrac