When you're done with your current set of changes to this file, you should call the read_lints tool with the specific file path and fix any newly introduced errors."},{"role":"assistant","content":[],"tool_calls":[{"id":"toolu_01GtVqH6HNhBbLSa1DFbPLUi","type":"function","function":{"name":"read_lints","arguments":"{"paths": ["app/src/main/java/com/afaneca/myfin/ui/common/nav/NavigationState.kt"]}"}}]},{"role":"tool","name":"read_lints","tool_call_id":"toolu_01GtVqH6HNhBbLSa1DFbPLUi","content":"No linter errors found in 1 checked files."},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me explain what was wrong:

## The Root Cause

The issue was in `stacksInUse`. It was always including both the `startRoute` (Login) and the current `topLevelRoute` (Transactions) in the entries list:

```kotlin
// OLD - WRONG
stacksInUse = [Login, Transactions]
```

